    detailedInstructions:'1) Compose the worst prompt you can for a real task: vague, no context, buried intent. 2) Run it and enjoy the mess. 3) List the 5 specific things wrong with it. 4) Fix them ONE at a time, re-running after each fix and noting what changed. 5) Rank the fixes by impact — that ranking is your personal prompting priority order.',
